==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=Maquis}}

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|fr|maquis}}, from {{der|en|co|machja}} (related to {{cog|it|macchia}}), ultimately from {{der|en|la|macula}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈmakiː/|/maˈkiː/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|botany}} Dense [[Mediterranean]] [[coastal]] [[scrub]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#* {{quote-journal|date=May 27, 2007|author=Alida Becker|title=Season in the Sun|work=New York Times|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2007/05/27/books/review/becker-t.html
|passage=The older man claims to find a measure of peace in Corsica’s wild landscape, and as Mitchell explores the foothills of '''maquis''', fragrant with “the sharp resinous smell of laurel rose and thyme,” he too succumbs.}}
# {{lb|en|historical}} The French [[resistance]] movement during World War II, or other similar [[movement]]s elsewhere. {{defdate|from 1940s}}
#* '''1977''', {{w|Alistair Horne}}, ''A Savage War of Peace'', New York Review Books 2006, page 75:
#*: By this time O.S. membership numbered some 4,500, and many of those who escaped imprisonment either fled abroad or formed the nucleus of a growing '''maquis''' in the more inaccessible parts of the country.

